  abstract={This chapter explores the emerging field of adopting artifical intelligence (AI)/machine learning (ML)-powered textual analysis for instructional improvement within the structure of the Instructional Core Framework. It reviews existing studies on AI/ML applications in analyzing teacher, student, and content data, emphasizing the transformative potential of technologies like large language models (LLMs) and generative AI in enhancing instructional efficiency and effectiveness. Through case studies, it illustrates how these technologies can provide actionable insights and generate new instructional materials, thereby advancing professional development, classroom observations, student assessments, and content analysis. The chapter concludes with future research directions, advocating for the integration of AI/ML methodologies with educational domain knowledge to foster an adaptive, inclusive, and equitable educational ecosystem.},
